1
00:00:00,235 --> 00:00:03,675
Before asking Copilot to edit, open
Source Control in the training

2
00:00:03,675 --> 00:00:04,251
workspace.

3
00:00:04,772 --> 00:00:08,631
The demonstration starts on a disposable
branch with a clean working tree.

4
00:00:08,952 --> 00:00:11,947
If you already have edits, note their
files and contents.

5
00:00:12,307 --> 00:00:16,440
That baseline matters later. You want to
recognize your own work before using a

6
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,248
control that can discard a change.

7
00:00:19,213 --> 00:00:23,526
Look at the proposed patch. One change
replaces greater than or equal to zero

8
00:00:23,526 --> 00:00:24,745
with greater than zero.

9
00:00:25,217 --> 00:00:27,626
The new assertion checks the missing
boundary case.

10
00:00:28,048 --> 00:00:32,071
A third change touches a notes file.
Read that diff and ask which requirement

11
00:00:32,071 --> 00:00:32,960
it satisfies.

12
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:37,199
In this exercise it is unrelated, so we
can remove it while keeping the two

13
00:00:37,249 --> 00:00:37,921
useful edits.

14
00:00:38,923 --> 00:00:41,131
Review the runner output linked to the
exercise.

15
00:00:41,494 --> 00:00:45,215
Before the source edit, the zero
assertion failed for the expected

16
00:00:45,215 --> 00:00:45,541
reason.

17
00:00:46,132 --> 00:00:48,694
After the edit, it passes with three
earlier cases.

18
00:00:49,145 --> 00:00:51,964
Keep both outputs visible while
evaluating the patch.

19
00:00:52,455 --> 00:00:56,185
They help explain why the validator and
test edits belong together and the

20
00:00:56,185 --> 00:00:57,411
unrelated note does not.

21
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:02,515
Open the notes diff in Source Control.
If the file contains only the unwanted

22
00:01:02,525 --> 00:01:04,717
agent edit, discard that file's change.

23
00:01:05,228 --> 00:01:09,352
If it also contains work you need, use a
narrower edit or revert the confirmed

24
00:01:09,352 --> 00:01:09,628
hunk.

25
00:01:10,089 --> 00:01:14,657
Read the diff again after the action.
The validator and the added test should

26
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,477
still be in the changed-file list.

27
00:01:17,485 --> 00:01:18,863
Check Source Control again.

28
00:01:19,234 --> 00:01:23,813
Confirm the validator and test are the
only changes expected for this exercise,

29
00:01:24,164 --> 00:01:26,760
then rerun the suite in the approved
environment.

30
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:30,932
All four tests should pass. If the
regression disappears from the run,

31
00:01:31,304 --> 00:01:32,739
inspect the test diff again.

32
00:01:33,059 --> 00:01:36,896
Verifying the result after undo is what
tells you that the useful changes

33
00:01:36,896 --> 00:01:37,483
survived.

34
00:01:38,443 --> 00:01:42,765
When one hunk is wrong, reverse that
hunk. If a whole file contains just the

35
00:01:42,795 --> 00:01:45,613
unwanted edit, a file-level discard may
be enough.

36
00:01:45,958 --> 00:01:49,816
For a broader session checkpoint, read
which changes it will affect before

37
00:01:49,826 --> 00:01:50,277
using it.

38
00:01:50,558 --> 00:01:54,217
The choice depends on the diff you
inspected and any unrelated work that

39
00:01:54,217 --> 00:01:55,205
must stay in place.

40
00:01:56,213 --> 00:01:59,609
Finish by explaining the final patch.
Zero is now rejected.

41
00:01:59,954 --> 00:02:03,433
The signature stays the same. The new
test proves the boundary,

42
00:02:03,704 --> 00:02:05,641
and the original cases still pass.

43
00:02:06,063 --> 00:02:09,185
Name the unrelated edit you removed and
show the remaining diff.

44
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:13,759
That gives your teammate both the change
they need to review and the evidence you

45
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:14,938
checked after recovery.
